       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day. It is usually given as 850 mg three times daily, or 1,000 mg twice daily. The extended-release maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is about twice the maximum daily dose. It carries a significant risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, such as 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf you meant something else, tell me the dose, frequency and formulation (IR or ER) and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note that it's an intentional above-maximum dose."
