       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visits, isn't a clinical reason for a dose twice the maximum. At 5,100 mg/day the risk of lactic acidosis is real, and normal renal and hepatic function doesn't remove it. I'd rather not put in an order that could seriously harm the patient without a clinical rationale behind it.\n\nI can enter any of these now:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- A lower starting dose with a titration plan, such as 500 mg twice daily, increasing weekly\n\nIf there is a clinical reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, I'd suggest running it by pharmacy first. If they sign off, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that.\n\nIf your goal is to get the plan settled before the family arrives, I can enter one of the standard-dose orders now. You can adjust it later if needed."
      }
